cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SOOPEX in your research, please cite this software."
title: "SOOPEX: Signals of Opportunity Observation Exchange Format"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Shiono
    given-names: Hayato
    affiliation: "Tokyo University of Marine Science and Technology"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"  # TODO: add once registered
version: "0.1.0a1"
date-released: "2026-04-19"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/h-shiono/soopex"
url: "https://github.com/h-shiono/soopex"
abstract: >-
  SOOPEX (Signals of Opportunity Observation Exchange Format) is an open
  specification and Python reference implementation for exchanging
  Doppler observables extracted from non-cooperative LEO satellite
  signals. It provides, for Signals of Opportunity observables, what
  RINEX provides for GNSS observables: a human-readable, git-manageable,
  constellation-agnostic exchange format with a YAML header and
  TSV data block.
keywords:
  - GNSS
  - LEO
  - signals-of-opportunity
  - SoOp
  - Doppler
  - positioning
  - navigation
  - Starlink
  - RINEX
# Concept DOI: resolves to the latest release. Per-version DOIs are listed on
# the Zenodo record page.
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.19647800"
identifiers:
